    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "300 insertions each of the Lippes loop intrauterine device, the Copper T device, and the Dalkon shield were evaluated in postabortion patients from June through October 1973. The incidence of light bleeding, pain, pain with bleeding, and backache was similar for all devices at early follow-up, although the Lippes loop had a slightly lower overall incidence of side effects than the Copper T and the Dalkin shield. The aggregated clinical and interview data indicate 310 terminations. Women with previous Lippes loop experience tolerated all 3 devices as well as other women did, and had fewer terminations when a loop was inserted postabortally."
    }
